    <statement><p>Find the simplest vector parametric expression <m>\vec{r}(t)</m> for the line that passes through the points <m>P = \left(-3,-1,1\right)</m> at time t = 4 and <m>Q = \left(-1,4,3\right)</m> at time t = 9.</p>
<p><m>\vec{r}(t) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(-3,-1,1\right)+\left(t-4\right)\mathopen{}\left&lt;0.4,1,0.4\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
